# order — the system's files, in the order the interpreter compiles them. A file that is not named
# here does not load: Berry resolves a global when it compiles a file, so a class has to be a global
# by the time a file that names it is compiled.
records.be
ux.be
components/component.be
components/icon.be
components/text.be
components/layout.be
components/progress_bar.be
components/scrollbar.be
components/pressure_display.be
components/duration.be
# The band the ux component draws: a layout of cells, so it loads after the components.
overlay.be
scene.be
list.be
# The registry registers registrations, and the routines below the system extend the record.
registration.be
registry.be
settings/settings.be
settings/view.be
settings/edit_scene.be
settings/edit_cfg.be
settings/bool.be
settings/choice.be
# The one kind with no scene of its own: a number is the base editor.
settings/number.be
settings/pressure.be
settings/duration.be
settings/settings_edit.be
# The jingle row extends the choice kind, so it follows it.
settings/jingle.be
# The device's own set is built from the kinds above, the jingle row included.
settings/device.be
# The browser's Forward opens the settings list, and its rows come from the registry.
browser.be
# The home scene's run, which home.be holds.
home_machine.be
# Last: it names browserScene in its gestures and DeviceSettings in the list it opens.
home.be
